    {
      "id": "claim_acc810142d1640f191efece6da7aaf71",
      "statement": "The auto-approval drainer applies eligible pending actions in ascending id order with a per-gatekeeper single-flight guard (a concurrent drain sets a rerun flag rather than running twice, since the DO's input gate is open across the apply await); eligibility requires both the author's autoApprovable verdict and a user-enabled rule, the drain stops at the first manual-gate action rather than skipping ahead, re-reads each record before applying to guard against concurrent drains, and a failed apply leaves the action pending and stops the drain.",
